{"story_id":"IN-58816-025","title":"The Adventures of a Bird","title_raw":"THE ADVENTURES OF A BIRD","notes":"","language":"en","original_language":"und","country":"India","country_code":"IN","culture_region":"ヒマラヤ山麓","latitude":31.1,"longitude":77.2,"location_precision":"culture_region","map_location_type":"source_culture_region","collector":"Alice Elizabeth Dracott","translator":null,"publication_year":1906,"year_evidence":"扉に 1906(序文は 1905 年 4 月の採録に触れる)","book_id":"PG-58816","book_title":"Simla Village Tales, or Folk Tales from the Himalayas","source_provider":"Project Gutenberg","source_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/58816","source_title":"Simla Village Tales; Or, Folk Tales from the Himalayas","license_status":"PUBLIC_DOMAIN_US","license_name":"Public Domain (United States)","license_jurisdiction":"US","rights_evidence_url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/ebooks/58816","redistribution_allowed":true,"commercial_use":true,"derivative_use":true,"ml_processing_status":"reviewed","verification_date":"2026-09-08","word_count":213,"text":"A small bird was once half buried in a puddle and could not escape,\nso it called to a passing stranger for help.\n\n\"Take me out, O stranger, and as a reward, you may eat me when my\nfeathers are dried.\"\n\nSo the man assisted it; but no sooner were its wings free than it\nflew away without expressing a word of gratitude.\n\nAfter going a short distance it found a cowrie (or small shell,\nthe smallest current coin in India, and now very rarely used), and\njoyously exclaimed: \"I have found a cowrie, I have money--I am now\nhigher than a Rajah.\"\n\nA Rajah hearing this, sent a man to take away the cowrie. \"See,\"\nsaid he, \"that bird says it is higher than a Rajah.\"\n\nSo he took the cowrie, and brought it to the Rajah.\n\nWhereupon the bird said: \"See, that Rajah was hungry, so he took away\nmy money.\"\n\nThis annoyed the Rajah so much (as only the poorest people deal in\ncowries) that he immediately restored it to the bird, who, nothing\ndaunted, replied: \"See, the Rajah was afraid, and so he has returned\nmy cowrie.\"\n\nThis was going a little too far, and the Rajah, in a rage, ordered\nthe offender to be shot.\n\nMoral.--Let Well alone.","cluster":8,"analysis":{"analysis_version":"1.0","embedding_model":"intfloat/multilingual-e5-small","themes":[],"motifs":[],"animals":[{"label":"鳥","count":4,"method":"count","confidence":1.0}],"nature":[{"label":"海","count":3,"method":"count","confidence":1.0}],"events":[{"position":0.0,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":0.091,"label":"Reward","hits":1,"lift":180.79,"method":"count"},{"position":0.182,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":0.273,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":0.364,"label":"Encounter","hits":1,"lift":52.95,"method":"count"},{"position":0.455,"label":"Encounter","hits":1,"lift":52.95,"method":"count"},{"position":0.545,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":0.636,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":0.727,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":0.818,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":0.909,"label":null,"hits":0,"lift":0.0,"method":"count"},{"position":1.0,"label":"Return","hits":1,"lift":84.96,"method":"count"}],"tension":[{"position":0.0,"tension":1.0,"raw":5.882,"method":"lexicon"},{"position":0.091,"tension":0.0,"raw":0.0,"method":"lexicon"},{"position":0.182,"tension":0.0,"raw":0.0,"method":"lexicon"},{"position":0.273,"tension":0.0,"raw":0.0,"method":"lexicon"},{"position":0.364,"tension":0.0,"raw":0.0,"method":"lexicon"},{"position":0.455,"tension":0.0,"raw":0.0,"method":"lexicon"},{"position":0.545,"tension":0.0,"raw":0.0,"method":"lexicon"},{"position":0.636,"tension":0.0,"raw":0.0,"method":"lexicon"},{"position":0.727,"tension":0.0,"raw":0.0,"method":"lexicon"},{"position":0.818,"tension":0.0,"raw":0.0,"method":"lexicon"},{"position":0.